Name: systemThemeName

Type: property

Syntax: get the systemThemeName

Summary:
Returns the name of the current GTK theme on Linux.

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: linux

Platforms: desktop

Example:
if the systemThemeName contains "dark" then
    set the backColor of me to "black"
    set the foreColor of me to "white"
else
    set the backColor of me to "white"
    set the foreColor of me to "black"
end if

Description:
The <systemThemeName> property returns the name of the active GTK theme as
reported by the system, for example "Menta" or "Arc-Dark". On platforms other
than Linux this property returns empty.

References: systemAppearance (property), systemWindowColor (property), systemTextColor (property), systemAppearanceChanged (message)
